          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Twistor space
            in the original sense of (
            %a{:href => "#Penrose67"}> Penrose 67
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+geometry"} complex geometry
            is usefully related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+geometry"} conformal geometry
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+compactification"} conformally compactified
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexification"} complexified
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %em Penrose transform
            from twistor space to this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            yields powerful computational tools for studying certain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            classes on twistor space to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+Yang-Mills+theory"} self-dual Yang-Mills fields
            on spacetime (
            %a{:href => "#Ward77"}> Ward 77
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#WardWells90"} Ward-Wells 90
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+string+theory"} twistor string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MHV+amplitudes"} MHV amplitudes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Witten03"}> Witten 03
            ).
          %p
            This
            %em Penrose transform
            is exhibited by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannians"} Grassmannians
            which is a special case of general such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            as they are studied in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schubert+calculus"} Schubert calculus
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+representation+theory"} geometric representation theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            and “generalized Penrose transforms” to be those induced by the relevant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BastonEastwood89"} Baston-Eastwood 89
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Cap01"} Cap 01
          %p
            In this generality given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+subgroups"} parabolic subgroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_2
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1 \cap P_2
            %em twistor correspondence
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            (see also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Schubert+calculus#Correspondences"} Schubert calculus – Correspondences
            and at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horocycle+correspondence"} horocycle correspondence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ∩
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; G/(P_1 \cap P_2)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{p_1}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}
                  \\\
                  G/P_1 &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; G/P_2
                  }
          %p
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projections"} projections
            onto the two
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            and a
            %em Penrose transform
            is an
            = succeed "/pull-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+transform"} integral transform
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} push
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_2)_! \circ (p_1)^\ast
            through this correspondence.
          %p
            In particular there are higher twistor spaces corresponding to higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetimes"} Minkowski spacetimes
            which are useful for describing higher dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            (
            %a{:href => "#MREIC11"}> MREIC 11
            ) with its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+field"} self-dual higher gauge field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            \.
          %p
            The original
            %em twistor correspondence
            (
            %a{:href => "#Penrose67"}> Penrose 67
            ) is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
          .maruku-equation
